  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_2c32b9631c56421bb384ff8e57a0775e",
      "statement": "The Go API and the Python agent are configured from a single shared YAML file, which Docker Compose mounts into both containers at /app/config.yaml and points each service at with the inres_CONFIG_PATH environment variable.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy/docker/docker-compose.yaml#L108-L126",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c5423afa73df09cea046643314c528b643314328a92172b04d80b4cb61311b49:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy/docker/docker-compose.yaml#L59-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3a90ac8543e9ad53cc280f2c71da0a388d9fe6adf0c07c381f2139c4119f6342:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_77b0ac3099ec43fabbc69da6ed9a1fc3",
      "statement": "Both services resolve configuration with the precedence environment variables over YAML file over built-in defaults.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/config/settings.py#L239-L262",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:68da9921e97ec149e0d202d45d2e1518432c8fcab1333be812c954ecca08fe27:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/config/settings.py#L84-L90",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ab9e5466d786055afe85ad3bc82f7fa93f4d1114107ff6766ef65ec805a66374:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/internal/config/config.go#L62-L127",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:05cffd418477970d1a7a69ecb0fc435935981dc789c42fa4bc5de0b0177d403d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_48698edd7774434b950067e7d0ef0b6d",
      "statement": "The Go loader tolerates a missing config file by logging and continuing with defaults and environment variables, but returns any other config-read error as fatal, so a malformed file fails loudly rather than silently falling back.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/internal/config/config.go#L128-L137",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d49ad34bbbcdfb409914597252d62f6c9ca248f1ddd75fe5c0ba3dfda71fd9fc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3f04b64332e04aa99043d0f828ad63cf",
      "statement": "The Go loader reads a .env file if present purely as a local-development convenience so that 'go run' works without manually exporting variables, and ignores its absence because production and Docker deployments have none.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/internal/config/config.go#L64-L72",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c631a7590e860b4acd01ad29e77b045ecc5fbc94ca964540be88f4303c6c14f1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6f231b472fec4bfd952cc3e4ceec262c",
      "statement": "The Python agent searches for its config file in inres_CONFIG_PATH first and then a fixed list of fallback paths, and an inres_CONFIG_PATH that names a nonexistent file logs a warning and falls through to those fallbacks rather than failing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/config/settings.py#L205-L235",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:27c742d209ce5b9c041de5f84a66c7ad3945ecb6b5d6e7020f315be061d7e18c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_249fc5d4b0524897a6b02d63e7ab5724",
      "statement": "Both services write their resolved configuration back into the process environment because a large amount of existing code reads environment variables directly rather than the configuration object.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/config/loader.py#L44-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d6b7c4e6e15e26bada0a08728f05520fcd2eef29651e24ee638bcba84e8f079a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/internal/config/config.go#L138-L172",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:90abb5861517fe83cc54b26a9671baef67c52cdba86dc1e764a98b5ee829eb98:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_935551d87e324f09bc70569da2b503ce",
      "statement": "The Go backfill writes each environment variable only when it is currently empty, so an explicitly exported variable is never overwritten by a value from the YAML file and the environment-wins precedence holds even for code that never reads the Config struct.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/internal/config/config.go#L170-L176",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2401c178c0d4bc2a75dbed809735f64335d876c7969e29422a38a5bdc78d4774:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ae58e4cfc2b24cee94de489f4725ebd8",
      "statement": "The Go loader binds conventional environment variable names such as DATABASE_URL, REDIS_URL, PORT, SUPABASE_URL and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY explicitly, so Docker and Kubernetes deployments need not use the legacy inres_ prefix, while the notification gateway keeps prefixed names inres_CLOUD_URL, inres_CLOUD_TOKEN and inres_INSTANCE_ID.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/internal/config/config.go#L88-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:703df788dce0127f837a7a03e18d43e4c47f5a75d05d18cd0080b0e5b4794e1e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_81255e5a14c64cf18bcf52d294990402",
      "statement": "The configuration test pins that standard environment variables populate the config struct and that inres_CLOUD_URL reaches the nested notification gateway configuration.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/internal/config/config_test.go#L10-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:253e45c6189fab26c322cf8b0b6e2c050a8362655849b98f5120d763d0b7b7c4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9ece3cb44816415dadf2676c39fb9a4a",
      "statement": "A database URL is mandatory: the API server logs a fatal error and exits when database_url is unset, because the background workers cannot run without Postgres.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/cmd/server/main.go#L36-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7d94694d3ce9d0b60d5aa4fcf22f36ab6d5b03254ba8e7a8409892f23a75d37f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/cmd/worker/main.go#L28-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bff65541c52ffc37e54b3c60ec6333d7f9c790fce99646e59561c4403af8e141:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d8b1c8e0b37b4f029d2ebd85282bacaa",
      "statement": "supabase_jwt_secret is optional and needed only for legacy HS256 tokens, because current Supabase projects issue ES256/RS256 tokens verified against a JWKS public key.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy/docker/volumes/config/cfg.ex.yaml#L44-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f5373d78aaf188fb1816617b4677f07b87ee821912b6a497ef170771d6c1e3bb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f2e91df3e71d4387b370630530d38988",
      "statement": "Redis is optional for the API server: it tries the configured URL, falls back to probing localhost:6379, and on failure logs that it is running without Redis and continues with a nil client rather than exiting.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/cmd/server/main.go#L62-L91",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4c982be3920b9c9ebff83ded6ecbd986ed46386204e153a7660a8ddac4c2ba78:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d24bcc5b0c8341f5a61b8a504d625202",
      "statement": "The notification gateway is required only for mobile push notifications; cloud relay registration is gated on IsConfigured() and runs in a background goroutine whose failure is logged as a warning, so an unreachable relay cannot delay or block API startup.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy/docker/volumes/config/cfg.ex.yaml#L49-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d229230492851dcd3655058b320947e41453b8e057254e62b4a5c9404d6cdaa:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/router/api.go#L66-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:45a6f3eac43121594a9e14c4a923bee6aed27693f1fbf4f07b476c65b381b661:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d900a95d3836472e8d1aa4e7a4870d1f",
      "statement": "Identity service initialization failure and analytics queue creation failure are both logged as warnings rather than aborting router construction, so the API starts with those capabilities degraded instead of not starting at all.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/router/api.go#L72-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2570d2222c860e04d1ad20223cc5b35a3e0d60a1d462afdb4e0b169056f2adef:"
